  "notes": "Mosley Music songwriter turned artist (The Clutch), across the Timbaland / Danja / Polow board, 2008–2010. The research gives \"75–95 straight/half-time plus a 125 club outlier\", and the straight band is the base because the entry's drum grammar is a backbeat one — \"snare pushed off the backbeat\" only means something against 2 and 4. Three drum deltas: \"kick clusters on 16ths\" at three to five hits a bar with the highest syncopation in this batch (0.7) and a 0.28 tresillo lean; the snare pushed 6–13 ms off the grid, an order past the parent's 1–4; and \"clicky non-hat percussion\" as a four-lane perc/perc2/woodblock/rim bed at −4 dB against a hat lane cut to 0.2. \"The Danja cuts add a four-on-the-floor-adjacent electro kick and a gated clap\", hence `fourOnFloorInChorus` and the clap stack. Harmony is \"two- to four-chord minor vamps with 'low electronic lines' carrying the melodic bed\", so the counter is at −12 with `arp` leading at a 0.5 density — the electronic line is the counter, not a pad. \"Her writer's instinct shows in dense, syllable-packed hooks\" is a 5–12 melody density with a 0.86 step share; \"pre-choruses that strip the drums entirely\" is the authored prechorus in the structures with a high `dropOutBeats`. The low end is \"808 sub with slides on the R&B cuts; a saturated electro synth-bass in 8ths on the Danja productions\" — both bass parts, so no `drums.bass808` block, and the rhythm is `offbeat_8ths` with a real glide. ⚠ The research marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]` and it is repeated here: the F♯-minor reading is inferred from a sibling record on the same board, not from this one. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `F#m`, and the remaining values `Cm`, `Bm`, `Gm`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
